          <p class="eyebrow mb-3">Overview</p>
          <h2 class="section-title">Quantum-ready cryptography, today</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose-content">
          <p>The cryptographic landscape is shifting. RSA and ECC — the algorithms securing virtually all digital communications, financial transactions, and government data today — are founded on mathematical problems that quantum computers are expected to eventually solve. Data encrypted now under classical cryptography can be stored and decrypted later when quantum capability arrives. This means that data requiring long-term confidentiality is already at risk.</p>
          <p>MEAICON addresses this through a layered post-quantum security architecture: hardware-rooted cryptographic keys that never leave silicon, fully homomorphic encryption enabling computation on encrypted data, multi-party computation distributing key material across multiple parties, and zero-knowledge proofs providing verifiable audit without data exposure. The result is cryptographic agility — the ability to adapt to evolving standards without architectural disruption.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

