<h2 id="post-quantum-security">Post-Quantum Security</h2>
<h2 id="meaicon-llc-fz-post-quantum-security">MEAICON LLC FZ – Post-Quantum Security</h2>
<p><strong>Positioning:</strong> MEAICON LLC FZ leads the adoption of <strong>Post-Quantum Cryptography (PQC)</strong> to future‑proof critical infrastructure against quantum computing threats.</p>
<h2 id="why-meaicon">Why MEAICON</h2>
<p>As quantum computers mature, classical asymmetric algorithms (RSA, ECC) become vulnerable. MEAICON proactively implements PQC algorithms to safeguard data confidentiality and integrity:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>NIST‑Standardized PQC Algorithms</strong> – Integration of Kyber (key encapsulation) and Dilithium (digital signatures) for forward secrecy.</li>
<li><strong>Hybrid Encryption</strong> – Classical + PQC cipher suites during transition period.</li>
<li><strong>Quantum‑Resistant Key Management</strong> – Safe rotation and distribution of PQC keys across edge nodes.</li>
<li><strong>Threat‑Adjusted Risk Management</strong> – Continuous monitoring of quantum‑computing capability evolution.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="key-capabilities">Key Capabilities</h2>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>PQC Algorithm Suite</strong></td>
<td>Kyber‑768, Dilithium‑3 for encryption and signatures.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Hybrid Key Exchange</strong></td>
<td>Combines classical ECDH with PQC KEM for transitional security.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Quantum‑Resistant Key Management</strong></td>
<td>Automated PKI updates and certificate lifecycle management.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Risk Assessment Framework</strong></td>
<td>Quantitative modeling of quantum threat vectors.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Compliance Support</strong> – Aligns with NIST PQC standardization roadmap.</td>
<td></td>
</tr>
</tbody>

